By the definition of $H$,
 $|f(\Gamma_{H}(w_1))|= |f(\Gamma_{H}(w_2))| = \Delta$. We define a special color $\alpha$ as follows. If
$f(w_2u_2)\in f(\Gamma_{H}(w_1))$, then let $\alpha:=f(w_2u_2)$. Otherwise,
$f(\Gamma_{H}(w_1))\setminus f(\Gamma_{H}(w_{2}))\neq \emptyset$, and we let $\alpha$ be any color in this difference.
