at least one such edge $u_2u'_2$ and $\alpha\neq f(w_2u_2)$, then we start by letting $f(u_2u'_2)=\alpha$. 
After coloring all pendant edges incident to $u_2$, we have 
\begin{equation}\label{0830}
 \mbox{\em $d_G(u_2)=2$ or $N^2_{G}[u_1z]$ has two edges of color $\alpha$ for each $1_G$-neighbor $z$ of $u_1$.}
