by~\eqref{0830}, if $d_G(u_2)\geq 3$, then  $M(u_1z)\leq |N^2_{G}[u_1z]\setminus\{u_1z\}|-1$. In any case,
$$M(u_1z)\leq d_{G}(w_1)+\max\{2, d_{G}(u_2)-1\}+ (d_{G}(u_1)-3)\leq \Delta+\max\{2,\Delta-1\}+(\Delta-3)=3\Delta-4.$$
So we can always  find a free color for $u_1z$.
This yields a $(3\Delta-3)$-coloring of $G$, a contradiction.
This shows that $u_1$ is special, and by symmetry, this also shows that $u_2$ is special.
